WEBVTT

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:55.440
I guess I'll have to dry
them at the apartment.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:57.440
The weather's nice.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:08.520
Nice weather, but that
clothes line is a dangerous place.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:18.590
Strange old man.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:45.980
What is that
old guy doing?

00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:59.330
Add water slowly--

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:01.870
Oh dear. Did I
put in too much?

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:03.200
Manager?

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:05.170
Yes?

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:08.610
What is it?

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:11.640
What!?
A strange man?

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:16.050
Some sleazy-looking middle-aged
type, wearing dark glasses.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:18.480
I'll go see.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.160
M-Manager,
it's too dangerous!

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:24.990
What if he's some
kind of predator?

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.690
I'll be fine.
I'm just going to look.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:39.540
Nobody's here.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.300
That's weird.

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:44.510
Hey!

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.060
You! Hiding behind
the telephone pole!

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:50.470
What do you want!?

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:52.680
Come back!

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:56.820
See, Manager?
Wasn't he suspicious?

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:59.750
He could have been a
burglar, or an arsonist!

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:02.190
Is that what
he looked like?

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:06.540
An underwear thief! With a
face like that, there's no doubt!

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:08.930
You think so?

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:12.370
He had this perverted
look on his face!

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:13.840
R-Really?

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:19.390
Next time
I'm calling the cops!

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:22.020
--He--
--Yeah?

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:23.550
He's--

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.660
He's my father.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.220
F-Fa--

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:38.460
Y-You're kidding--

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:42.070
When I saw him
run away, I was sure.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:46.800
Sorry to trouble you.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.670
I--
I see.

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:52.150
I knew he was an
upstanding gentleman!

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:55.110
Full of middle-aged
mature style.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.350
It's a natural mistake.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:00.890
The way he was
sneaking around.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.560
It seems there's
more to this story.

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.870
Kozue, have you ever had
a fight with your dad?

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:21.680
Why would you
want to know that?

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:24.550
No reason in particular.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:29.710
I was wondering about
father-daughter relationships.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:35.960
Dad's kind of at a loss
what to do with me.

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:38.720
Maybe he's shy--

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:43.160
Let's say,
only for instance...

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:46.500
...his daughter married
against his wishes.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.840
What would your father do?

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:54.210
My father would
approve of you!

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:57.050
I'm sure you two
would get along!

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:02.610
Daddy always said I should
bring my boyfriends over.

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:05.890
He wants to be sure nobody
would ever make me cry.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:09.320
And if he still
didn't like the guy?

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.760
You're right.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:15.530
He might be stubborn,
saying we're too young.

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:19.720
Are we having the
same conversation?

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:36.680
Maybe I'll call them.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:46.020
Forget it!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.790
I know what
they'll say, anyway.

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:50.400
"Come home."

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:53.240
"Get remarried."

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:55.530
I know the script.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.040
Hello, Maison Ikkoku--

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:05.240
Mother?

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:07.220
Your father never
spoke to you?

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:11.040
But you know what
he was there for.

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:14.750
What?
He ran away!?

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:19.960
It was so embarrassing! A
tenant thought he was a stalker!

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:21.690
Stalker?

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:26.320
Dear, you said Kyoko wasn't
there. Did you lie to me?

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:28.330
What?

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:30.340
What's this all about?

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:33.940
Not on the phone. Come
over next Sunday and we'll--

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:39.480
Don't be difficult. You never
came home for New Year's.

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.680
You'll be here?
We'll be waiting.

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:49.620
Let's hear it.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:52.290
Why'd you run away?

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:55.470
What's the big deal? I saw
the aparrtment, didn't I?

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:59.870
Dear, it's that attitude
that keeps Kyoko away.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:01.000
What?

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:04.810
You fought her
marriage tooth and nail.

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:07.240
We couldn't
back down later.

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:09.640
It was all in
Kyoko's best interests.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:11.310
So this Sunday--

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:16.710
And see? Soichiro died only
months after the wedding!

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:19.010
If she had chosen a
healthy young man--

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:22.000
Will you quit harping
on what's over and done!?

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:24.130
Stop it or I'll
divorce you!

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:27.170
Ritsuko, wait!

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:41.940
I hate this!
What should I do?

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:45.880
And judging from Daddy's
looks, he's still mad at me.

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:53.150
I should just smile.

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:56.960
And keep the
conversation light.

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:01.220
Smile like that
and say...

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:03.960
..."I'm home, Daddy!"

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:10.060
H-Hello.
Welcome back, Kyoko.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:14.110
And what does that mean?

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:16.410
Are you telling
me to quit my job?

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:19.780
Well, basically, yes.

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:24.280
A broken-down apartment
is no place for a young girl.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:29.220
Now you're being rude!
That place is where I work!

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:34.490
Kyoko, this isn't about
how the apartment looks.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:38.700
Soichiro's father is
the landlord, right?

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:43.230
You shouldn't lean on your
dead husband's family forever.

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:45.460
You're a burden!

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:46.780
How?

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:53.920
He may be a "tenant," but you can't
be seen living with a young man!

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:55.380
"Young man"?

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:58.120
Do you mean Godai?

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:00.430
His name is
beside the point!

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:04.090
My unmarried daughter will
never become damaged goods!

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:05.890
Meaning what, exactly!?

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:07.260
You're coming home!

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:08.390
No!

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:10.530
Let's make this clear.

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:14.300
I am not working because of
any obligation to the Otonashis.

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:17.330
I happen to
like it there!

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:21.940
So I won't quit!

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:26.580
Kyoko! Why don't you listen
to your parents for a change!

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:30.680
If you don't like it, then
just call me an orphan!

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:32.720
Let's not--
Kyoko!

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:36.530
Just where do you
get that "charm"?

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:40.320
Anyway, you are going
to quit Maison Ikkoku!

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:42.770
--No
--I'm not listening!

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:43.960
Kyoko!

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:46.200
Look look at
your posture!

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:48.270
I told you, no!

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:50.340
I told you, I'm
not listening!

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:51.940
I-said-no!

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:53.980
I'm-not-listening!

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:55.880
T-That's enough, you two.

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:56.710
What!?

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:58.180
What, Daddy!?

00:11:43.670 --> 00:11:44.930
A broken-down apartment?

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:52.990
Maybe, but it's home.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:58.780
That's right!
This place is home!

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:03.100
Tomorrow, I'll
work really hard!

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:35.740
So you're fixin' it?

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:39.200
It's just emergency
repairs, but--

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:42.070
I'll help you.

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:43.210
No thanks.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:46.210
I'd like to do it myself.

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:50.250
A waste of effort, though.

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:52.320
The wood's rotten
straight through.

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:54.720
What do you think?

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:57.590
I guess it'll
hold for now.

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:00.320
--No, not there!
--No, not there!

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:04.230
M-Manager!

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:15.040
F-Fine, I'll call
a contractor.

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:18.440
Right. Good idea.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.480
All right, the
apartment is broken-down.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:29.330
But thinking it over,
the tenants are nice people!

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:36.330
What? Godai and the manager
got physical on the balcony?

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:38.500
Yeah, first thing
in the morning!

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:40.100
That's love!

00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:41.070
Right!

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:44.530
They pay their rent--

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:46.940
Manager?

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:48.050
Y-Yes?

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:52.710
Could you be somewhat
patient with my rent this month?

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:55.720
Is it impossible?

00:13:57.090 --> 00:13:58.750
I-I'll be patient.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.520
--For a LITTLE while.
--Thanks.

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:05.260
It's like he was waiting
For that moment.

00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:15.430
But I'm not beat yet.
I should be used to it by now.

00:14:17.350 --> 00:14:20.440
Huh? What's
everybody looking at?

00:14:21.050 --> 00:14:24.910
I'll never quit! Not as long
as Maison Ikkoku stands!

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:28.190
Hey! Those're termites!

00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:30.490
I knew it!

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:32.940
This building
is done for.

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:08.560
Are you going to spray
every room in the building?

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:12.420
No. I'll just spray
and coat the outside.

00:15:13.670 --> 00:15:14.460
Thank goodness.

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:20.970
What's all the racket
so early in the morning!?

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:23.510
The contractors are here.

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:28.110
You guys are such slobs!

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:31.980
Finally fixing
the clothesline?

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:34.880
Yeah. And outside they're
spraying for termites.

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:37.480
So she's serious.

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:41.580
She said to tell her if
there's anything else to fix.

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:47.560
I'll tell her to fix
the holes in my walls.

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:53.300
Good morning.

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:54.760
Outta the way.

00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:59.500
I refuse. How
cruel you are, Godai!

00:15:59.820 --> 00:16:00.750
Why?

00:16:02.220 --> 00:16:07.590
That hole is the social link
between the two of us.

00:16:07.890 --> 00:16:11.550
I don't wanna
be "linked"!

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:14.820
Don't mind this.
Get back to work.

00:16:17.070 --> 00:16:19.560
You wound me, Godai!

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:23.700
I thought we
were soul-mates!

00:16:23.770 --> 00:16:24.820
Who is!?

00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:27.440
I treasure that hole!

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:29.530
It's an invasion
of privacy!

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:36.080
You are determined
to close it?

00:16:36.150 --> 00:16:37.670
Yes!
I'm closing it!

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:43.290
I hear Godai's voice
crying out at midnight!

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:46.150
What can he be saying?

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:48.850
I prick up my ears.

00:16:49.930 --> 00:16:52.990
"Kyoko!."

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:56.660
Those are his very words.

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:00.430
And heavy breathing.

00:17:00.510 --> 00:17:01.530
Yotsuya!

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:04.310
So I peep through the hole.

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:06.570
And I see...

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:10.680
...nothing.
It is far too dark.

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:16.720
What is he doing at midnight,
calling the manager's name?

00:17:17.060 --> 00:17:18.750
I ponder.

00:17:18.830 --> 00:17:21.690
What I do in my
room is my business!

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:25.500
How depressin'.
One youth shot to hell.

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:26.620
Painful.

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:29.370
I shall inform
the manager.

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:30.900
Go ahead.

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:34.470
I never expected
resistance.

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:36.960
I won't be
intimidated.

00:17:39.650 --> 00:17:41.810
Guys, this ain't
live theater.

00:17:42.550 --> 00:17:44.070
Yeah, this is better!

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:51.080
You greatly
underestimate me.

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:58.560
Godai pictures the manager
in his disgusting fantasies!

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:02.100
She can't hear
that outside!

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:10.740
But she can hear
it from the landing.

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:18.280
Something wrong,
Young Godai?

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:20.490
Godai!

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:21.150
Yes?

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:25.020
I'll call the plasterer. You
make your room presentable.

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:27.190
Manager!

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:31.420
I've been meaning to fix
it for some time now.

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:35.360
You're confusing the issue. Godai
is using you for his disgusting--

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:39.000
If we fix it, you won't have to
ponder over any strange sounds!

00:18:39.980 --> 00:18:41.530
I'm in hell.

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:43.760
Thank you!

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:48.180
Well, that's that.

00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:54.010
What else should I fix up?

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:05.460
This place is a long way
from the wrecking ball!

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:08.230
And the termites weren't
so much of a problem.

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:16.370
Hello, Maison Ikkoku--

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:19.900
It's just you, Mother.

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:22.040
What do you
mean, "just"?

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:25.340
Is that any
way to speak?

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:32.220
Your father and I have been
talking about you quitting.

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:35.980
I told you,
I'm not quitting!

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:39.520
We decided that we should be
the ones to tell Mr. Otonashi.

00:19:39.770 --> 00:19:40.790
Stop that!

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:52.770
We're doing this
for your own good!

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:57.140
If you say one word to Mr.
Otonashi, I'll disown you!

00:19:57.720 --> 00:19:58.740
Mark my words!

00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:05.220
I'm your daughter,
not your slave!

00:20:06.730 --> 00:20:07.950
I'm not to
be trifled with!

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:13.990
A parent is not
to be trifled with!

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:26.710
Yo!

00:20:28.480 --> 00:20:29.410
Headin' home?

00:20:29.690 --> 00:20:32.120
Yeah.
Out shopping?

00:20:32.390 --> 00:20:34.290
Yep. Gotta
make dinner.

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:39.180
Don't you think the
manager's acting weird lately?

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:41.250
So worked up
about the apartment.

00:20:41.930 --> 00:20:43.420
Isn't it
better that way?

00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:46.790
It's just kinda sudden.

00:20:47.770 --> 00:20:49.930
You may be right.

00:20:50.440 --> 00:20:53.770
See? You've
noticed it, too!

00:20:54.680 --> 00:20:56.510
Something's up.

00:20:57.980 --> 00:20:58.670
"Something"?

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:21.290
We're home!

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:25.090
What's the
matter, Soichiro?

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:32.100
You got no dinner, yet?

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:33.740
Hold on.

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:35.610
Here.

00:21:37.720 --> 00:21:42.310
The Manager never forgets
to feed him. Did she go out?

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:45.780
She's probably
ordering more repairs.

00:22:16.290 --> 00:22:17.450
Anyone home?

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:21.020
Who is it?

00:22:22.100 --> 00:22:24.090
I--
I'm--

00:22:26.440 --> 00:22:28.560
Kyoko Otonashi's mother.

00:22:30.440 --> 00:22:33.460
I've come to tender my
regards to the tenants.

00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:35.430
"To the tenants"?

00:22:35.910 --> 00:22:37.240
What is the matter?

00:22:37.550 --> 00:22:38.240
Dunno.

00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:51.850
I'd like to thank you for
your kindness to my daughter.

00:23:04.710 --> 00:23:11.010
As of today, Kyoko has resigned
her position at Maison Ikkoku.

00:23:26.060 --> 00:23:26.450
Re--

00:23:28.030 --> 00:23:30.190
Resigned?

00:23:49.650 --> 00:23:52.770
Thank you all for
worrying about me.

00:23:53.660 --> 00:23:55.890
I have no intention
of resigning.

00:23:56.760 --> 00:23:57.380
But--

00:23:58.290 --> 00:24:02.810
Next: "Kyoko's Brush with Danger!
Mother's Nefarious Plot"

00:24:03.770 --> 00:24:06.460
I will be Maison Ikkoku's
manager forever!
